import LiZhongQC.Basic

/-!
# Shared layer: the Borel σ-algebra of the extended plane

The extended plane `ℂ̄ = LiZhongQC.ExtPlane` (`OnePoint ℂ`) carries no `MeasurableSpace` instance in Mathlib or in the
project. Works that put measures on subsets of `ℂ̄` (harmonic measure on the boundary of a domain of `ℂ̄`,
Garnett–Marshall 2005 I.3 and II.1) use its Borel σ-algebra, provided here as **scoped** instances in namespace
`References` (DESIGN §2, shared layer; registry `refs_lean\FOUNDATIONS.md`).

Usage: `open scoped References` activates the instances (so do a plain `open References` and `namespace References`);
a selective `open References (…)` does not. Pommerenke 1992 writes the same σ-algebra explicitly as
`MeasurableSet[borel ExtPlane]`.

* Shared notion (the Borel σ-algebra of `ℂ̄`, with its `BorelSpace` structure) — `extPlaneMeasurableSpace`,
  `extPlaneBorelSpace`
-/

namespace References

open LiZhongQC

/-- The Borel σ-algebra of the extended plane `ℂ̄`, the σ-algebra generated by its open sets. Scoped: it is active
only after `open scoped References`. -/
noncomputable scoped instance extPlaneMeasurableSpace : MeasurableSpace ExtPlane := borel ExtPlane

/-- The σ-algebra `extPlaneMeasurableSpace` is the Borel σ-algebra of `ℂ̄` (scoped with it). -/
scoped instance extPlaneBorelSpace : BorelSpace ExtPlane := ⟨rfl⟩

end References
